              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for maturity, then the Tamil for negligence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: சாது",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சாது — cātu — \"a meek person; a gentle soul\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "என் தாத்தா ஒரு சாது, அவருக்குக் கோபமே வராது. eṉ tāttā oru cātu, avarukkuk kōpamē varātu. My grandfather is a gentle soul; he never gets angry."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a holy man; சாதுவான மாடு, a docile cow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சாது (cātu) is borrowed from Sanskrit sādhu, \"straight, good; a good man\" (CDIAL 13337)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
